    },
    {
      "sha": "92fcd2f50df11436a60c2941c252e9cbaf7c692b",
      "node_id": "C_kwDOM2nIG9oAKDkyZmNkMmY1MGRmMTE0MzZhNjBjMjk0MWMyNTJlOWNiYWY3YzY5MmI",
      "commit": {
        "author": {
          "name": "Den Delimarsky",
          "email": "den@anthropic.com",
          "date": "2026-07-28T16:08:12Z"
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Den Delimarsky",
          "email": "den@anthropic.com",
          "date": "2026-07-28T16:08:12Z"
        },
        "message": "Skip redirect sources that already exist when cutting a release\n\nThe nav patch step in cut-release adds a dated sibling redirect for\nevery /specification/draft/... entry, but it never checked whether that\ndated source was already present. When main already carries the\n<version>/ redirects, the loop appends a second copy of each source and\nMintlify rejects the resulting docs.json for reusing a source path,\nwhich is exactly what broke the 2026-07-28 release PR. Track the\nexisting sources in a set and skip any collision so the step is\nidempotent regardless of what main already contains.\n\n:house: Remote-Dev: homespace",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "5db86d53f63b12bf6a8e26041ff9756385b1330f",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/trees/5db86d53f63b12bf6a8e26041ff9756385b1330f"
        },
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/commits/92fcd2f50df11436a60c2941c252e9cbaf7c692b",
        "comment_count": 0,
        "verification": {
          "verified": true,
          "reason": "valid",
          "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPbA7dhvWZS1Fisg2EUXUGynMp8\nD1nASMs2SeJ65r+akAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQN9dJJpxQCpWiXkT5xsUOOtfbOV9EPI3SO+OXPe0iREWwJW1YHPPv18eOM3EM9iGWZ\nzLi9nHfSIF5SQ9imVZgAc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----",
          "payload": "tree 5db86d53f63b12bf6a8e26041ff9756385b1330f\nparent bbcfe53e15195b66ba7f87719f100bc1c0ecee31\nauthor Den Delimarsky <den@anthropic.com> 1785254892 +0000\ncommitter Den Delimarsky <den@anthropic.com> 1785254892 +0000\n\nSkip redirect sources that already exist when cutting a release\n\nThe nav patch step in cut-release adds a dated sibling redirect for\nevery /specification/draft/... entry, but it never checked whether that\ndated source was already present. When main already carries the\n<version>/ redirects, the loop appends a second copy of each source and\nMintlify rejects the resulting docs.json for reusing a source path,\nwhich is exactly what broke the 2026-07-28 release PR. Track the\nexisting sources in a set and skip any collision so the step is\nidempotent regardless of what main already contains.\n\n:house: Remote-Dev: homespace\n",
          "verified_at": "2026-07-28T16:08:14Z"
        }
      },
