    {
      "sha": "73763114e511106fc07543f6096b3a814b1a3583",
      "node_id": "C_kwDOM2nIG9oAKDczNzYzMTE0ZTUxMTEwNmZjMDc1NDNmNjA5NmIzYTgxNGIxYTM1ODM",
      "commit": {
        "author": {
          "name": "gjz22",
          "email": "33962655+gjz22@users.noreply.github.com",
          "date": "2026-07-31T02:18:07Z"
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "GitHub",
          "email": "noreply@github.com",
          "date": "2026-07-31T02:18:07Z"
        },
        "message": "fix(scripts): parse wrapped Author(s) lines in render-seps (#3178)\n\nThe Author(s) regex used `.` to capture the field value, which does not\nmatch newlines. When an author list wrapped onto an indented continuation\nline, every author after the first line was silently dropped from the\ngenerated docs/seps/*.mdx table, leaving a dangling comma in the cell.\n\nCapture the first line plus any indented continuation lines that do not\nbegin a new list item, and collapse interior whitespace when the value is\nused. Regenerated the three affected SEP documents: 2322 (was losing 1 of\n3 authors), 1865 (6 of 9), and 2575 (2 of 5).\n\nCo-authored-by: Gabriel Zimmerman <gabez@Gabriels-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "436eaedc9232f06b45c61e7cb7a7ac8e15e62eb5",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/trees/436eaedc9232f06b45c61e7cb7a7ac8e15e62eb5"
        },
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/commits/73763114e511106fc07543f6096b3a814b1a3583",
        "comment_count": 0,
        "verification": {
          "verified": true,
          "reason": "valid",
          "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbAXfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjc0QAK5T/GO00smNIBv2ytmyrs6+\n1Qg3I/osFKtdJexzARgAUAm4obPNq7Emcy7CIh0FZ9jDS/HudHCWaXOwDOt/wvQx\nQw61FwexonXu/x63PURjfx6bV7/jhF9ewR+miepLDDrh4zZoPQQR2enmREmhIE5l\nl2Y+2Wd2O6K05PirEtEyo9zNi1aby7/zMWSZ8hwimUtK9vsJsTgVDtsaN9SCzIwa\nurDi8ZIULwOYPev6g2zJTAVTjHRhAcmPziVYUB1fZOsxT2zqNQXKbrTWxykh2Z0F\nwi4yIaPh2L1TtiSPJYvjhXMYW//9Ab+fouE5cve+eMDpyFsQONOHB/MOX03UY9M7\nMkO4QsW00fk+CLFARVrIXZCK5c0N6wq6//pJJ7t3QnI7A78/s02fbcH7GKn0o9r4\nFASk2MjcfbpfN+XZc5vstkRI7kGBdBUXy4SXeGXBU56BovQ12zZgU/psyG/McJ5B\nQjyLGayHUPzzODjBXQ1V7c766X3b6k8BlkpK0ZUxrpYbMubbEOLfT+9FwKqacmVJ\nZZzPItGjJV8PCJzipXC62yMk3tTF9NOy5pPQn63fvcnTc7DgtUyDqO5oNbsoZG/B\n7yJFcIMks45vUEdCd/pILQt89X4/l/XaMvwlKky/NLYBrpugNFow8NHJgiucTVIz\nNAHhsQuzrTTCSyZq3R2+\n=+/H8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
          "payload": "tree 436eaedc9232f06b45c61e7cb7a7ac8e15e62eb5\nparent 41d9e938e9a9edf23a69429be180cad172e00f4e\nauthor gjz22 <33962655+gjz22@users.noreply.github.com> 1785464287 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785464287 -0600\n\nfix(scripts): parse wrapped Author(s) lines in render-seps (#3178)\n\nThe Author(s) regex used `.` to capture the field value, which does not\nmatch newlines. When an author list wrapped onto an indented continuation\nline, every author after the first line was silently dropped from the\ngenerated docs/seps/*.mdx table, leaving a dangling comma in the cell.\n\nCapture the first line plus any indented continuation lines that do not\nbegin a new list item, and collapse interior whitespace when the value is\nused. Regenerated the three affected SEP documents: 2322 (was losing 1 of\n3 authors), 1865 (6 of 9), and 2575 (2 of 5).\n\nCo-authored-by: Gabriel Zimmerman <gabez@Gabriels-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "verified_at": "2026-07-31T02:18:07Z"
        }
      },
