    {
      "sha": "881ee6559065460fc21429c38fb818c81ca07ea6",
      "node_id": "C_kwDOM2nIG9oAKDg4MWVlNjU1OTA2NTQ2MGZjMjE0MjljMzhmYjgxOGM4MWNhMDdlYTY",
      "commit": {
        "author": {
          "name": "olaservo",
          "email": "olahungerford@gmail.com",
          "date": "2026-08-14T18:18:02Z"
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "olaservo",
          "email": "olahungerford@gmail.com",
          "date": "2026-08-14T18:18:02Z"
        },
        "message": "Patch two high-severity advisories in dev dependencies\n\nBoth are transitive, lockfile-only, and within the ranges their parents\nalready declare, so no direct dependency moves.\n\n- fast-uri 3.1.4 -> 3.1.5 (CVE-2026-18446, GHSA-7p8r-x3mc-p8w7): host\n  confusion via a backslash authority introducer. Reaches the tree through\n  ajv, which declares ^3.0.1. This is Dependabot alert #90, open since\n  2026-08-04.\n- brace-expansion 5.0.8 -> 5.0.9 (GHSA-rgw5-rvv9-x895): DoS via unbounded\n  intermediate arrays, bypassing the CVE-2026-14257 mitigation. Reaches the\n  tree through eslint -> minimatch. Not reported by Dependabot.\n\n`npm audit` now reports 0 vulnerabilities. Verified the consumers of both\npackages still work: `eslint schema/` is clean and\n`tsx scripts/validate-examples.ts` passes 258/258.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "92c13c73f0ceae64a0bccbbf9edf3c3c2f1addd0",
