    {
      "sha": "4b0368a25d4767dba8842e918aacb407b11e0a8c",
      "node_id": "C_kwDOM2nIG9oAKDRiMDM2OGEyNWQ0NzY3ZGJhODg0MmU5MThhYWNiNDA3YjExZTBhOGM",
      "commit": {
        "author": {
          "name": "Peter Alexander",
          "email": "pja@anthropic.com",
          "date": "2026-08-20T13:00:42Z"
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Peter Alexander",
          "email": "pja@anthropic.com",
          "date": "2026-08-20T13:00:42Z"
        },
        "message": "SEP-2640: make (server, URI) the identity of a skill and require materialized paths to encode it\n\nThe SEP said a skill is identified by its URI, which holds only within\none server: two connected servers may both serve\nskill://refunds/SKILL.md, and those are unrelated skills. State that\nthe identity of an MCP-served skill is the pair of the host's identity\nfor the originating server and the skill URI, and that hosts must\npreserve both halves in the registry, persisted approvals, the cache,\nand any tool or path the model reaches the skill through.\n\nRequire any path at which a host materializes skill content, whether a\ncache directory or a virtual mount, to encode the server identity as\nwell as the URI, so same-URI skills from different servers land at\ndistinct paths and the originating server is recoverable from the\npath. Note in the host integration sketch that a virtual mount is one\nroot per server.\n\nRegenerate the rendered SEP docs.\n\nNo-Verification-Needed: documentation-only change",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "0dc5fb6957f3c96eac5de43fb5d269d3ac219a82",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/trees/0dc5fb6957f3c96eac5de43fb5d269d3ac219a82"
        },
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/commits/4b0368a25d4767dba8842e918aacb407b11e0a8c",
        "comment_count": 0,
        "verification": {
          "verified": true,
          "reason": "valid",
          "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3TEOWZgs8wFZnafNMjeE03DAzR\nEZQ3QjwTbkVfb2zV8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNkuz+/MWnwgKC5073wGBMEz1Va8OL2CcQ+vHj1VGEM0Q7sdIYlpzHCzf1Ox2mXCaV\nGkTbZKWsepn9BxCpeDbQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----",
          "payload": "tree 0dc5fb6957f3c96eac5de43fb5d269d3ac219a82\nparent a9834326e77fe7c79bc8a1dc7f8871ae8ff85bf2\nauthor Peter Alexander <pja@anthropic.com> 1787230842 +0000\ncommitter Peter Alexander <pja@anthropic.com> 1787230842 +0000\n\nSEP-2640: make (server, URI) the identity of a skill and require materialized paths to encode it\n\nThe SEP said a skill is identified by its URI, which holds only within\none server: two connected servers may both serve\nskill://refunds/SKILL.md, and those are unrelated skills. State that\nthe identity of an MCP-served skill is the pair of the host's identity\nfor the originating server and the skill URI, and that hosts must\npreserve both halves in the registry, persisted approvals, the cache,\nand any tool or path the model reaches the skill through.\n\nRequire any path at which a host materializes skill content, whether a\ncache directory or a virtual mount, to encode the server identity as\nwell as the URI, so same-URI skills from different servers land at\ndistinct paths and the originating server is recoverable from the\npath. Note in the host integration sketch that a virtual mount is one\nroot per server.\n\nRegenerate the rendered SEP docs.\n\nNo-Verification-Needed: documentation-only change\n",
          "verified_at": "2026-08-20T13:55:45Z"
        }
      },
