          "email": "ahmadyaseen35@gmail.com",
          "date": "2026-08-21T23:20:57Z"
        },
        "message": "docs: align safe-integer justification with tools.mdx\n\nThe x-mcp-header integer bound is justified as \"the safe range for JavaScript\" here and as the IEEE754 double-precision range in server/tools.mdx. Same constraint, same numeric range, two different justifications. The IEEE754 phrasing was agreed in the review of #2772; the revision landed in tools.mdx but not here.\n\nNo normative change: the bound is untouched.",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "2dd8d405fdf8579ab05ec314390d63bd9a3e2ab2",
