    {
      "sha": "00c3f2e7885870a6b8261c670e7efbc9b1a4a886",
      "node_id": "C_kwDOM2nIG9oAKDAwYzNmMmU3ODg1ODcwYTZiODI2MWM2NzBlN2VmYmM5YjFhNGE4ODY",
      "commit": {
        "author": {
          "name": "Den",
          "email": "53200638+localden@users.noreply.github.com",
          "date": "2026-09-22T13:08:33Z"
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "GitHub",
          "email": "noreply@github.com",
          "date": "2026-09-22T13:08:33Z"
        },
        "message": "Use loopback IP literals in the CIMD redirect_uris example (#3384)\n\nRFC 8252 Section 8.3 recommends the loopback IP literal over\n`localhost` for native-app redirect URIs, since `localhost` can resolve\nto non-loopback interfaces and is more exposed to local firewall and\nresolver misconfiguration. The example metadata document listed both\n`127.0.0.1` and `localhost`; swap the `localhost` entry for the IPv6\nloopback `[::1]` and update the sequence diagram to match.\n\nThis only touches the non-normative example in the draft spec.\n\nReported by @adeinega. Fixes #3223",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "4107ce93513b018faf587730c09c57296d6ad8fe",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/trees/4107ce93513b018faf587730c09c57296d6ad8fe"
        },
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/git/commits/00c3f2e7885870a6b8261c670e7efbc9b1a4a886",
        "comment_count": 0,
        "verification": {
          "verified": true,
          "reason": "valid",
          "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsn3SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjQQQAEWXD4I/VZymBbq8y/Y0+7NM\nC2s3VW7j0sMmxhoEQRTM9QFeYVlBbaLSj/iLUkPUBIPGIffr60nH1em29gMRewI6\nVjVgER0Ad2uoUE1gnIu9cmrCVb0eIgIPltei/DjbLIylQk2qqvK9/PNtorDWF6TU\nRCriFffgQvdK//2mwiBog0P3Wcub/ebh/VA1zP6+1ujgJeYiP9e+9lkZXAWvCKoA\nHHsnnb8yZNWxlWFDDbP878BOYkPXNpgghQN7LzzAkpJfXr4HQboHmrX4bOBr/KUb\nDTmP8O56rR0KjYfYmnuJybsp7b9YzrrV4p5OK/y+C21oJmQ5idkubgeyzqCbGm3E\ndSy9uZmUDY1q5XiMztr2o1cB4PiZNsd2UNHv+2pGXKLakhaEHJl4RuAM7wB+fxKv\nrDn6ICliHCk0MtkR0038DZkALKKaYib5OgDtglEiLWyIHuaItQ3uatngcZU4YwGY\n4+JrWkfSfj9OkiKx7+i6Qk9HtE/7nMFcvwsu2uNtpihs83rJuadTLEw+i1VVtvsz\nBGivyjvjLm7iBFqqepMr2ZmmlO/GOc2EEy2V6589kfQ5N6WA0ZxUcZEyjGd9s+Gv\nBye2ltolXNgfk9bCdxz1LhZjMrjSdEDVhxAo94R19JYKBTxgkM/h5fuSvmLmTdGZ\nfk62QgTJGa2QKthkHtxn\n=sMqJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
          "payload": "tree 4107ce93513b018faf587730c09c57296d6ad8fe\nparent d91f73c06bc21f111747670b003a501bdc68ee10\nauthor Den <53200638+localden@users.noreply.github.com> 1790082513 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790082513 +0000\n\nUse loopback IP literals in the CIMD redirect_uris example (#3384)\n\nRFC 8252 Section 8.3 recommends the loopback IP literal over\n`localhost` for native-app redirect URIs, since `localhost` can resolve\nto non-loopback interfaces and is more exposed to local firewall and\nresolver misconfiguration. The example metadata document listed both\n`127.0.0.1` and `localhost`; swap the `localhost` entry for the IPv6\nloopback `[::1]` and update the sequence diagram to match.\n\nThis only touches the non-normative example in the draft spec.\n\nReported by @adeinega. Fixes #3223",
          "verified_at": "2026-09-22T13:08:35Z"
        }
      },
