      "blob_url": "https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/blob/75db1e987cbbba6d170315dc99d0dfc440754aef/docs%2Fdocs%2Fdraft%2Fgetting-started%2Fintro.mdx",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/raw/75db1e987cbbba6d170315dc99d0dfc440754aef/docs%2Fdocs%2Fdraft%2Fgetting-started%2Fintro.mdx",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/contents/docs%2Fdocs%2Fdraft%2Fgetting-started%2Fintro.mdx?ref=75db1e987cbbba6d170315dc99d0dfc440754aef",
      "patch": "@@ -25,8 +25,8 @@ Think of MCP like a USB-C port for AI applications. Just as USB-C provides a sta\n Depending on where you sit in the ecosystem, MCP can have a range of benefits.\n \n - **Developers**: MCP reduces development time and complexity when building, or integrating with, an AI application or agent.\n-- **AI applications or agents**: MCP provides access to an ecosystem of data sources, tools and apps which will enhance capabilities and improve the end-user experience.\n-- **End-users**: MCP results in more capable AI applications or agents which can access your data and take actions on your behalf when necessary.\n+- **AI applications or agents**: MCP gives them access to an ecosystem of data sources, tools and apps, which enhances their capabilities and improves the end-user experience.\n+- **End-users**: MCP results in more capable AI applications or agents that can access user data and take actions on the user's behalf when necessary.\n \n ## Broad ecosystem support\n \n@@ -55,11 +55,23 @@ MCP is an open protocol supported across a wide range of clients and servers. AI\n ## Learn more\n \n <CardGroup cols={2}>\n+  <Card title=\"Architecture\" icon=\"book\" href=\"/docs/draft/learn/architecture\">\n+    Learn the core concepts and architecture of MCP\n+  </Card>\n+\n   <Card\n-    title=\"Understand concepts\"\n-    icon=\"book\"\n-    href=\"/docs/draft/learn/architecture\"\n+    title=\"Security\"\n+    icon=\"lock\"\n+    href=\"/docs/draft/tutorials/security/security_best_practices\"\n   >\n-    Learn the core concepts and architecture of MCP\n+    Understand the security considerations and best practices for MCP\n+  </Card>\n+</CardGroup>\n+\n+## Community\n+\n+<CardGroup cols={2}>\n+  <Card title=\"Contributing\" icon=\"users\" href=\"/community/contributing\">\n+    Learn how to get involved and contribute to MCP\n   </Card>\n </CardGroup>"
    },
